      "question": "What happens to Social Security in 2034?",
      "answer": "2034 is the year the combined retirement and disability trust funds would run out, if the two were treated as one. At that point benefits would be cut 17%, growing to 35% by 2100. The retirement fund on its own is projected to run short earlier, in 2032, and the cost of a fix would be about 15% larger by 2034."
